🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch
The general conversion utility Tensor.to(...) supports modification of all other tensor option fields except layout. This is a natural extension, and the lack of it will be felt more deeply as support for sparse layouts grows. In particular functions supporting sparse output generally accept an optional layout argument and contain the following pattern:
//Perform necessary steps to build the output in a `sparse_coo` representation
...
auto result_coo = at::sparse_coo_tensor(indices, values, shape);
if (layout) {
  if (*layout == Layout::SparseCsr) {
    return result_coo.to_sparse_csr();
  }
  if (*layout == Layout::SparseCsc) {
    return result_coo.to_sparse_csc();
  }
  ...
}
return result_coo;
This would simplify to:
//Perform necessary steps to build the output in a `sparse_coo` representation
...
auto result_coo = at::sparse_coo_tensor(indices, values, shape);
if (layout){
  return result_coo.to(*layout);
}
